```
// File: script.js
const screen = document.getElementById('screen');

function appendValue(value) {
  screen.value += value;
}

function clearScreen() {
  screen.value = '';
}

function deleteLast() {
  screen.value = screen.value.slice(0, -1);
}

function calculate() {
  try {
    if (screen.value.trim() === '') return;
    screen.value = Function(`"use strict"; return (${screen.value})`)();
  } catch (error) {
    screen.value = 'Error';
    setTimeout(() => {
      screen.value = '';
    }, 1200);
  }
}
```

Yeh JavaScript code calculator ke saare logic aur buttons ke click interactions ko handle karta hai. Iss code ka breakdown neeche diya gaya hai:

---

### 1. Screen Reference Select Karna
```javascript
const screen = document.getElementById('screen');
```
* **Kya karta hai:** HTML se calculator ki display screen (`id="screen"`) ko select karke `screen` naam ke variable me store karta hai taaki baaki functions me hum iski value read ya change kar sakein.

---

### 2. Value Input Karna (`appendValue`)
```javascript
function appendValue(value) {
  screen.value += value;
}
```
* **Kya karta hai:** Jab bhi koi number ya operator (+, -, *, /) click hota hai, yeh function us button ki `value` ko screen par chal rahe text ke aage jod (`+=`) deta hai.

---

### 3. Screen Clear Karna (`clearScreen`)
```javascript
function clearScreen() {
  screen.value = '';
}
```
* **Kya karta hai:** 'C' button click hone par screen ki value ko empty string (`''`) set karke poora display reset kar deta hai.

---

### 4. Ek Character Delete Karna (`deleteLast`)
```javascript
function deleteLast() {
  screen.value = screen.value.slice(0, -1);
}
```
* **Kya karta hai:** 'DEL' button click hone par `.slice(0, -1)` ka use karke screen par likhe text me se aakhri character (last digit ya operator) hata deta hai.

---

### 5. Calculation Perform Karna (`calculate`)
```javascript
function calculate() {
  try {
    if (screen.value.trim() === '') return;
    screen.value = Function(`"use strict"; return (${screen.value})`)();
  } catch (error) {
    screen.value = 'Error';
    setTimeout(() => {
      screen.value = '';
    }, 1200);
  }
}
```
* **`try { ... }` block:** 
  * Agar screen khali hai, toh function wahi ruka rehta hai (`return`).
  * `Function('"use strict"; return (...)')()` string expression ko mathematically calculate karta hai (yeh `eval()` se zyaada secure aur fast hota hai). Result seedhe screen par update ho jata hai.
* **`catch (error) { ... }` block:** 
  * Agar user koi galat expression daalta hai (jaise `5++2` ya `8/`), toh code crash hone ke bajaye screen par `'Error'` display karta hai.
  * `setTimeout` 1.2 seconds (1200ms) ke baad screen ko wapas clear kar deta hai.
